WEBVTT

00:00:16.850 --> 00:00:22.390
Perhaps as a result of living in the
humdrum world of a boarding school,

00:00:22.390 --> 00:00:28.440
I always wanted to see the outside world,
and attended university in Paris.

00:00:28.440 --> 00:00:33.950
There, I found a world of freedom
beyond my imagination.

00:00:36.740 --> 00:00:39.080
It was there that I...

00:00:42.500 --> 00:00:46.830
...became swept up in the fervour around
me, without fully understanding it,

00:00:46.830 --> 00:00:51.590
and participated in the university
clubs' student activism.

00:00:51.590 --> 00:00:58.890
In point of fact, the most that I ever did
was to distribute leaflets. However...

00:00:58.890 --> 00:01:00.680
I learnt that the organisation's officers

00:01:00.680 --> 00:01:04.270
were planning to engage
in subversive activities...

00:01:08.940 --> 00:01:14.570
Then, days ago, I was visited out of the
blue by a man calling himself Milverton,

00:01:14.570 --> 00:01:19.410
saying that he had a register from
the organisation with my name in it.

00:01:19.410 --> 00:01:25.370
J-Just a moment! When you say Milverton,
you mean the newspaper tycoon

00:01:25.370 --> 00:01:27.620
who runs many top-tier
media interests, don't you?

00:01:27.620 --> 00:01:30.250
Why would such a man approach you?

00:01:32.130 --> 00:01:34.840
I knew it.

00:01:34.840 --> 00:01:37.760
Charles Augustus Milverton--

00:01:37.760 --> 00:01:42.390
a man who has a second
persona unknown to the public.

00:01:42.390 --> 00:01:45.390
That being the king of blackmailers.

00:01:47.100 --> 00:01:51.320
This man Milverton is the kind of corrupt
vermin that takes so much pleasure

00:01:51.320 --> 00:01:56.070
in watching others fall to ruin...
he can't help himself.

00:01:56.070 --> 00:01:58.740
I'm not bothered by this, Mary.

00:01:58.740 --> 00:02:01.410
Even if this does become
divulged to the public,

00:02:01.410 --> 00:02:04.700
I won't back out of our marriage.

00:02:04.700 --> 00:02:06.160
That may be true for you, John,

00:02:06.160 --> 00:02:09.080
but the French government
will not be so forgiving.

00:02:09.080 --> 00:02:13.710
If she is extradited and you two
become physically separated,

00:02:13.710 --> 00:02:17.010
you will not be able
to lead a married life.

00:02:18.180 --> 00:02:21.260
But there is no more treasure, right?

00:02:21.260 --> 00:02:24.640
So there's no way to meet
this man's demand, is there?

00:02:33.440 --> 00:02:36.690
Timing so precise it almost seems planned.

00:02:57.970 --> 00:03:02.050
<i>Tripped up by your twisted words</i>

00:03:02.050 --> 00:03:05.810
<i>I can't fall asleep at night</i>

00:03:05.810 --> 00:03:09.940
<i>Transfixed by your gaze</i>

00:03:09.940 --> 00:03:12.980
<i>I feel your sickness inside</i>

00:03:12.980 --> 00:03:17.400
<i>Injured, I break down</i>

00:03:17.400 --> 00:03:20.780
<i>this never-ending punishment</i>

00:03:20.780 --> 00:03:25.160
<i>I feel your sins all the time</i>

00:03:25.160 --> 00:03:29.750
<i>It's inescapable, take me away</i>

00:03:29.750 --> 00:03:33.330
<i>I don't feel your love</i>
<i>But I can give you love</i>

00:03:33.330 --> 00:03:37.460
<i>Show me a dream that will stir me awake</i>

00:03:37.460 --> 00:03:41.090
<i>I don't feel your love</i>
<i>But I can give you love</i>

00:03:41.090 --> 00:03:45.220
<i>Whenever I awaken, you fall apart</i>

00:03:45.220 --> 00:03:48.310
<i>Someday... (Free your soul)</i>

00:03:48.310 --> 00:03:52.640
<i>Find me (Free your mind)</i>

00:03:52.640 --> 00:03:56.110
<i>Steal your heart (Free your soul)</i>

00:03:56.110 --> 00:03:59.990
<i>Endlessly (Free your mind)</i>

00:03:59.990 --> 00:04:02.780
<i>I will scream aloud</i>

00:04:10.750 --> 00:04:14.960
"The Two Criminals"

00:04:14.960 --> 00:04:20.130
How good of you to come all the
way here to my office, Mr Milverton.

00:04:20.130 --> 00:04:24.680
At last we meet, Mr Holmes.

00:04:26.430 --> 00:04:28.310
And who is this gentleman?

00:04:28.310 --> 00:04:30.680
John H. Watson.

00:04:30.680 --> 00:04:35.190
Ah, you are Miss Morstan's fiancé.

00:04:35.190 --> 00:04:38.320
This is quite the pretty business
we are in, isn't it?

00:04:38.320 --> 00:04:43.320
Confound this man and his
transparent demeanour!

00:04:43.320 --> 00:04:47.240
Now then, I have called on you
for but one purpose.

00:04:47.240 --> 00:04:52.830
I have received word that the treasure
of Agra is at the bottom of the Thames.

00:04:52.830 --> 00:04:55.210
Regarding that matter...

00:04:55.210 --> 00:05:00.630
...could I ask you to verify for me
that Miss Morstan's name...

00:05:00.630 --> 00:05:03.050
...is actually on that
organisation's register?

00:05:19.440 --> 00:05:20.860
Mary!

00:05:27.030 --> 00:05:29.160
You may have gathered that
without the damning register,

00:05:29.160 --> 00:05:32.790
I would have no grounds to
blackmail her in the first place.

00:05:32.790 --> 00:05:35.040
How unfortunate for you.

00:05:35.040 --> 00:05:41.420
That is, of course, merely a copy; the
real list is securely in my safekeeping.

00:05:41.420 --> 00:05:45.130
Now, as to our negotiations...

00:05:45.130 --> 00:05:48.890
...I haven't the slightest intention
of ceding one inch of ground.

00:05:48.890 --> 00:05:52.560
I will be staying at the Langham
until noon on Saturday.

00:05:52.560 --> 00:05:55.980
You have until I leave the hotel.

00:05:55.980 --> 00:06:00.190
Do exercise your utmost to dredge
the bottom of the Thames.

00:06:00.190 --> 00:06:02.570
Well, if you will excuse me...

00:06:09.110 --> 00:06:13.450
Damn! What a scoundrel that Milverton is!

00:06:14.870 --> 00:06:19.210
The real list is securely
in his safekeeping...

00:06:20.460 --> 00:06:26.550
When he stays in London, he always
rents out an entire floor of the Langham,

00:06:26.550 --> 00:06:28.930
but the evidentiary material
he uses for blackmail

00:06:28.930 --> 00:06:33.100
is always kept in his
oceanfront villa in Brighton.

00:06:38.440 --> 00:06:40.600
An eye for an eye...

00:06:40.600 --> 00:06:43.440
Before he returns,
I will sneak into his mansion

00:06:43.440 --> 00:06:46.280
and steal the evidence.
I'll handle everything.

00:06:46.280 --> 00:06:47.400
Good heavens!

00:06:47.400 --> 00:06:49.740
Let you handle everything?

00:06:49.740 --> 00:06:51.780
Don't be ridiculous, Sherlock!

00:06:51.780 --> 00:06:55.120
I'm coming with you!
I'm prepared to see this through!

00:06:55.120 --> 00:06:58.830
This matter was one of mine
and Mary's to begin with!

00:07:01.290 --> 00:07:07.550
We are partners, aren't we? Side by side,
both solving riddles and going to prison!

00:07:13.300 --> 00:07:15.220
So now I'm sharing a room
with you in gaol, too?

00:07:15.220 --> 00:07:17.680
That should prove interesting, to be sure.

00:07:17.680 --> 00:07:20.640
But I doubt we will have
that to look forward to.

00:07:22.020 --> 00:07:26.650
For you see, I have a gift
when it comes to crime, as well.

00:07:41.460 --> 00:07:43.040
There doesn't seem to be a route for us

00:07:43.040 --> 00:07:45.420
to approach from the east
without being seen.

00:07:45.420 --> 00:07:48.840
Just to be safe, we should
go around to the west...

00:07:48.840 --> 00:07:51.800
I just saw a flash of light.
First storey, west side.

00:07:51.800 --> 00:07:54.930
Huh? But no one is supposed to be here.

00:07:56.720 --> 00:08:01.270
Gunshots! Then there
really is someone here.

00:08:01.270 --> 00:08:03.520
What do we do, Sherlock?

00:08:18.080 --> 00:08:20.700
So that's what this is.

00:08:21.910 --> 00:08:24.120
I've misread the situation.

00:08:24.120 --> 00:08:26.670
Hmm? How do you mean?

00:08:26.670 --> 00:08:31.130
John, head back into town
and fetch the police.

00:08:31.130 --> 00:08:33.840
And what are you going to do?

00:08:33.840 --> 00:08:37.680
Stay here and survey the situation.
Once you've brought the police,

00:08:37.680 --> 00:08:41.770
we'll use their investigation as
a cover for us to bury the evidence.

00:08:41.770 --> 00:08:46.150
Very well. But see that you don't take
any action without me, Sherlock.

00:08:46.150 --> 00:08:49.400
Right. Hurry along, now.

00:09:05.960 --> 00:09:08.960
They really are having
a right proper shootout.

00:09:08.960 --> 00:09:11.760
Getting in through the first
storey will be difficult.

00:09:31.730 --> 00:09:34.780
Please, lower your gun.

00:09:39.780 --> 00:09:42.620
Let's both remain calm
about this, why don't we?

00:09:42.620 --> 00:09:46.250
Will you at least hear out
what I have to say?

00:09:52.590 --> 00:09:57.010
So, you're here. And right around
the time I expected you, too.

00:09:58.760 --> 00:10:03.770
If you had been any later, I would have
gotten a hole between my eyes,

00:10:03.770 --> 00:10:06.770
Sherlock Holmes.

00:10:06.770 --> 00:10:12.860
Since neither of you understand the
situation, I will explain it from the top.

00:10:12.860 --> 00:10:15.780
That won't be necessary.

00:10:15.780 --> 00:10:21.280
You certainly do operate in a tortuously
roundabout way, Milverton.

00:10:21.280 --> 00:10:28.460
You blackmailed John's fiancée Mary
to drag me into this affair.

00:10:28.460 --> 00:10:33.630
Then, you drove us into a corner,
such that there could be no resolution

00:10:33.630 --> 00:10:36.800
unless we wrestle away the evidence
you're blackmailing her with,

00:10:36.800 --> 00:10:38.800
to get me to come here.

00:10:41.220 --> 00:10:44.350
When I received the report that
you got the treasure of Agra

00:10:44.350 --> 00:10:47.430
to be thrown into the river,
as I anticipated you would,

00:10:47.430 --> 00:10:49.940
I must admit that I laughed.

00:10:49.940 --> 00:10:56.280
I'll assume that you got <i>him</i>
to come here in some similar fashion.

00:10:56.280 --> 00:10:58.070
You are correct.

00:10:58.070 --> 00:11:03.160
And you likely have a fair guess as to
the reason why I summoned you here.

00:11:03.160 --> 00:11:07.660
Your part in this, which is...

00:11:07.660 --> 00:11:12.250
...to arrest the man
who stands before you.

00:11:13.420 --> 00:11:15.460
Allow me to introduce you.

00:11:15.460 --> 00:11:20.550
This man is the greatest criminal
in the entire British Empire...

00:11:23.430 --> 00:11:25.600
...the Lord of Crime.

00:11:37.030 --> 00:11:43.660
This man is the Lord of Crime--
Professor William James Moriarty!

00:11:45.370 --> 00:11:49.540
It is a shame that there are
no spectators to this comedy.

00:11:49.540 --> 00:11:56.300
The symbols of London's light and darkness
are both present and accounted for.

00:12:01.180 --> 00:12:07.220
Tch, it looks like we've both drawn
a nettlesome opponent, huh, Louis?

00:12:08.060 --> 00:12:12.690
But then, upstairs, right about now,
both your boss and my boss,

00:12:12.690 --> 00:12:14.860
as well as one other guest,

00:12:14.860 --> 00:12:19.230
Sherlock Holmes, will be engaged
in a three-way standoff.

00:12:19.230 --> 00:12:21.150
Did you say Holmes?

00:12:21.150 --> 00:12:25.740
I was hoping to see their absurd
drama play out, myself.

00:12:25.740 --> 00:12:28.490
But we are mercenaries.

00:12:28.490 --> 00:12:35.460
Our job is to slow you down and buy
enough time until the final curtain.

00:12:37.960 --> 00:12:39.630
Brother...

00:12:39.630 --> 00:12:40.800
Now then,

00:12:40.800 --> 00:12:44.930
under the circumstances, there is but
a single choice that you can make.

00:12:44.930 --> 00:12:50.220
That being... to have the Lord of Crime
be arrested by the detective.

00:12:51.560 --> 00:12:56.310
Moriarty, if I die,
I have made arrangements

00:12:56.310 --> 00:13:00.150
to have it reported in my media
that you are the Lord of Crime.

00:13:00.150 --> 00:13:03.740
However, if you are willing to go quietly,

00:13:03.740 --> 00:13:07.370
then your identity will remain
completely confidential

00:13:07.370 --> 00:13:11.290
and I will transfer custody of you
over to the government.

00:13:11.290 --> 00:13:15.420
Further, I promise that I will see to it
that you will lack for nothing

00:13:15.420 --> 00:13:18.880
and live your life under house arrest.

00:13:18.880 --> 00:13:20.920
And you, Holmes...

00:13:20.920 --> 00:13:24.970
...unless you want your dear friend's
precious wedding to be cancelled,

00:13:24.970 --> 00:13:27.890
you will submit to do as I say.

00:13:27.890 --> 00:13:30.140
If you have any reason to doubt my word--

00:13:30.140 --> 00:13:33.520
No, I'm willing to believe you.

00:13:35.520 --> 00:13:39.980
Assuming your objective
was to create this situation,

00:13:39.980 --> 00:13:41.820
then as long as your
drama plays itself out,

00:13:41.820 --> 00:13:44.900
you will have no further
reason to blackmail Mary.

00:13:44.900 --> 00:13:49.120
That's right. Some commoner
girl with no news value

00:13:49.120 --> 00:13:52.740
meant nothing to me from the start.

00:13:52.740 --> 00:13:55.120
And as for you...

00:13:55.120 --> 00:13:57.750
...there is no way you are going to stand
face-to-face with a mass murderer

00:13:57.750 --> 00:14:01.630
and just let the opportunity
to catch him slip away from you.

00:14:01.630 --> 00:14:06.300
Now, arrest the Lord of Crime, Holmes!

00:14:11.640 --> 00:14:16.560
I am in a position of superiority
over both of you, in every regard.

00:14:16.560 --> 00:14:20.650
This is what it is to be unassailable!

00:14:26.740 --> 00:14:27.910
Are you finished?

00:14:27.910 --> 00:14:29.620
Huh?

00:14:29.620 --> 00:14:33.330
My word, you ramble on.

00:14:33.330 --> 00:14:39.790
If this is a comedy, then you aren't
the king, you're the jester.

00:14:39.790 --> 00:14:44.920
You know, you've really misread
the situation, Milverton.

00:14:44.920 --> 00:14:47.420
I've what?

00:14:47.420 --> 00:14:55.520
Liam, isn't that right? If you're here,
then that is indubitably the case.

00:14:58.850 --> 00:15:02.610
Isn't it, Liam?! I'm glad it was you!

00:15:02.610 --> 00:15:05.860
To be honest, I couldn't
bear it if it wasn't you.

00:15:05.860 --> 00:15:10.200
I wanted it to be you, and there
is no one else it could have been.

00:15:10.200 --> 00:15:14.990
Which is why I truly am pleased
that you are the one here right now.

00:15:18.040 --> 00:15:19.160
W--

00:15:19.160 --> 00:15:21.920
Wait... Wait, wait, wait, wait!

00:15:21.920 --> 00:15:26.340
What in heaven's name does this mean?
Don't tell me... Don't tell me they're...

00:15:26.340 --> 00:15:30.550
It can't be... There's no way
these two have been in contact!

00:15:30.550 --> 00:15:33.930
Regardless of them being a
detective and an arch criminal!

00:15:33.930 --> 00:15:37.180
Wh-What the devil are you talking about?!

00:15:37.180 --> 00:15:40.640
Answer me, Sherlock Holmes!

00:15:40.640 --> 00:15:45.400
Liam, I want to rescue my partner,
who is about to be married.

00:15:45.400 --> 00:15:48.900
I am fine with whatever
becomes of me in the process.

00:15:48.900 --> 00:15:51.280
How about you?

00:15:51.280 --> 00:15:54.620
Do you care if he reveals
your name to the world?

00:16:00.410 --> 00:16:04.790
No. This is what I always intended.

00:16:04.790 --> 00:16:07.880
Then we've reached our decision.

00:16:07.880 --> 00:16:13.930
Wait, Holmes! If you kill me,
th-that evidence will be made public!

00:16:13.930 --> 00:16:15.970
That's not true.

00:16:15.970 --> 00:16:20.230
You may have the proof, but you haven't
arranged for it to be published.

00:16:20.230 --> 00:16:24.980
You said yourself that Mary had
no news value, didn't you?

00:16:26.900 --> 00:16:31.030
I thought as much. Whenever anyone
sees through to your true self,

00:16:31.030 --> 00:16:34.160
you're prone to clenching
your back molars.

00:16:35.120 --> 00:16:37.030
Ha, there it is again.

00:16:38.410 --> 00:16:41.370
I-It's not possible...

00:16:41.370 --> 00:16:46.880
For not one, but <i>both </i>of them to make...
such an irrational decision as this is...

00:17:12.780 --> 00:17:16.160
Time for your exit, Milverton.

00:17:50.520 --> 00:17:57.570
Even now, after all this, I can't prove
for certain that you're the Lord of Crime.

00:17:57.570 --> 00:18:02.830
You set me up to be the hero who
exposes the misdeeds of the nobility.

00:18:02.830 --> 00:18:04.960
I was always a step behind you,

00:18:04.960 --> 00:18:08.250
and you had me dancing
in the palm of your hand.

00:18:13.550 --> 00:18:15.260
Still...

00:18:19.140 --> 00:18:25.480
...not even you would have supposed...
that I would kill Milverton, right?

00:18:27.640 --> 00:18:32.020
Not <i>everything </i>is going to go
according to your whim.

00:18:32.020 --> 00:18:33.980
I won't let it.

00:18:35.530 --> 00:18:38.910
The game is afoot in earnest now, Liam!

00:18:38.910 --> 00:18:41.580
I swear I will unravel
everything about you,

00:18:41.580 --> 00:18:44.410
and catch you in a manner
of my own choosing!

00:18:48.540 --> 00:18:54.130
My response to that challenge
is the same as before--

00:18:54.130 --> 00:18:58.510
"Catch me if you can, Sherlock."

00:19:03.100 --> 00:19:06.640
Yeah. That's a promise.

00:19:16.150 --> 00:19:20.360
It looks like my bloke Milverton
has gone and gotten killed.

00:19:20.360 --> 00:19:23.330
I have no reason to continue
having it out with you lot.

00:19:26.830 --> 00:19:31.960
Bye now, Louis. If possible,
I hope to never see you again.

00:19:33.170 --> 00:19:35.500
Milverton is dead.

00:19:36.420 --> 00:19:38.670
Where are Holmes and Brother?

00:19:46.520 --> 00:19:49.140
Mr Milverton...

00:19:57.730 --> 00:19:59.400
The villa!

00:20:01.950 --> 00:20:04.030
Sherlock!

00:20:04.030 --> 00:20:05.240
Are you all right?!

00:20:05.240 --> 00:20:08.830
Yes, John. I'm fine.

00:20:09.710 --> 00:20:13.880
I incinerated the evidence
against Mary. Rest at ease.

00:20:13.880 --> 00:20:15.670
Huh?

00:20:15.670 --> 00:20:18.840
Mr Holmes, what is
the meaning of all this?

00:20:18.840 --> 00:20:21.380
Please explain what is happening.

00:20:21.380 --> 00:20:24.010
Very well.

00:20:24.010 --> 00:20:29.140
It will take a while to detail all of it,
but the short answer is...

00:20:31.020 --> 00:20:36.520
...I used this gun to kill Milverton.
Go ahead and arrest me.

00:20:36.520 --> 00:20:39.280
Wh-What did you say?!

00:20:39.280 --> 00:20:42.360
John, I'm sorry.

00:20:42.360 --> 00:20:45.950
It doesn't look as though I can
make it to your wedding.

00:20:45.950 --> 00:20:48.490
We have no choice.
Take him in for the time being!

00:20:48.490 --> 00:20:49.830
Sir!

00:20:56.630 --> 00:21:02.050
I thought we were...
I thought we were partners...

00:21:03.010 --> 00:21:06.140
Sherlock!

00:21:15.650 --> 00:21:18.610
Despite being rid of Milverton,

00:21:18.610 --> 00:21:22.780
I allowed Holmes to become
his killer in the process.

00:21:22.780 --> 00:21:25.660
You aren't to blame for that, Brother.

00:21:25.660 --> 00:21:29.620
He killed Milverton for his own reasons.

00:21:30.990 --> 00:21:38.340
You know, Louis... I never meant to let
him become a murderer as soon as this.

00:21:38.340 --> 00:21:39.670
Huh?

00:21:39.670 --> 00:21:45.840
I thought that for him, killing a man
would be the highest hurdle to overcome.

00:21:49.510 --> 00:21:54.640
Once you kill a man,
killing another makes no difference.

00:21:54.640 --> 00:21:57.060
Which is to say...

00:21:57.060 --> 00:22:02.070
...he will, in all likelihood,
be coming...

00:22:02.070 --> 00:22:04.650
...to kill me.

00:22:07.410 --> 00:22:14.710
<i>Fate that over time changes</i>
<i>into chains of sorrow,</i>

00:22:14.710 --> 00:22:22.920
<i>leave me the light of rebirth</i>
<i>for the world ahead</i>

00:22:29.550 --> 00:22:33.520
<i>Struck by a frustration</i>
<i>I'd never experienced before,</i>

00:22:33.520 --> 00:22:36.890
<i>I feel lost, I feel lost</i>

00:22:36.890 --> 00:22:40.900
<i>The letters I dashed off</i>
<i>are all I remember</i>

00:22:40.900 --> 00:22:44.280
<i>It's all true, it's all true</i>

00:22:44.280 --> 00:22:51.700
<i>Witness as I forgo my forsaken future</i>
<i>with no regrets</i>

00:22:51.700 --> 00:23:00.290
<i>and you will win your intent</i>
<i>at the expense of becoming my pawn</i>

00:23:02.290 --> 00:23:08.090
<i>A scarlet thread fluttering in the wind</i>
<i>at five in the morning</i>

00:23:08.090 --> 00:23:14.350
<i>I'll recover my memories on the last day</i>

00:23:14.350 --> 00:23:17.140
<i>Hold me down till the end</i>

00:23:17.140 --> 00:23:22.810
<i>Finish by wiping away my sins,</i>

00:23:22.810 --> 00:23:29.490
<i>warning me to stay true if I desire beauty</i>

00:23:44.840 --> 00:23:51.760
Next time on <i>Moriarty the Patriot</i>:
"The Final Problem Act 1."
